{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfryezz9ebqBu82Mztoz2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The race is fixed. `tests/test_metrics.py` failed 3 of 3 runs before the change and passes 5 of 5 after it. I changed only `metrics/counter.py`, and I did not commit.\n\n**Root cause:** `incr` did an unlocked read, a `time.sleep(0)` that yields, then a write, so concurrent increments overwrote each other. `snapshot()` copied the dict with no coordination with writers.\n\n**The fix:**\n- **Per-name locks:** each counter name gets its own `threading.Lock`. A small `_table_lock` guards only the lock table, so increments to unrelated counters never contend.\n- **`incr`, `get`, `reset(name)`:** each takes the lock for its own name only.\n- **`snapshot()`:** takes every counter lock in sorted name order, then returns a plain `dict` copy. That gives a true point-in-time view. Deadlock is avoided because no other operation holds more than one counter lock at a time.\n- **`reset()` with no argument:** clears one name at a time rather than under one global lock, so it is not atomic across names. I chose that to avoid serialising everything. Say if you want it atomic.\n- **API:** unchanged. `incr`, `get`, `snapshot`, and `reset` keep their signatures and behaviour.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `pytest tests/test_metrics.py` passes on all 5 runs.\n- A stress run with 6 writer threads and 3 concurrent `snapshot()` readers raised no errors and totalled 18000, matching the expected count.\n- A quick manual check confirmed `snapshot()` returns a `dict` and that `reset` works for both a single name and all names.\n\n**Trade-off:** the per-name lock table is never pruned, so it grows with the number of distinct counter names. That is bounded by the names a service uses, so I left it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12294,"cache_read_input_tokens":37057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12294},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad055cd4-07f4-4dbb-bc11-4d9ed2ba49fe","uuid":"a9c3c2c0-e68d-46db-87b9-78a2c5d4eb8f","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:27:33.119Z","request_id":"req_011CfryezinEGQ6T1ESvwuYj"}
